# story/04-confrontation.scene — bible.md spine scene 6
# (Confrontation, the climax-weight Rill puzzle). Kept lines are
# cited inline with their source. See docs/canon/bible.md and
# docs/canon/kept.md.

== confrontation
bg relay_point
show terminal static right
> The Terminal's own channel answers back, in a voice no login ever granted.
# kept: script.rpy:475
rustler: (Sh-greetings troubleshooter sh-your services sh-no longer required)
choice
    "Ask them why." -> rustler_why
    "Cut the channel now." -> rustler_cut

== rustler_why
# kept: script.rpy:481
rustler: (Sh-we are sh-cdr collective sh-we liberate data from sh-closed loops)
# kept: script.rpy:487
rustler: (Sh-not stealing sh-redistributing sh-information wants to be free sh-cargo wants to be free)
set rustler_sympathy += 1
-> confrontation_check

== rustler_cut
> Slim doesn't answer. The channel stays open anyway - it was never asking permission.
-> confrontation_check

== confrontation_check
check cosmonaut vs 4
    style -> hold_style
    success -> hold_ok
    tie -> hold_ok
    fail -> hold_hard

== hold_style
show slim talk left
slim: Not today.
-> find_signal_puzzle

== hold_ok
> Slim keeps the channel open, hands steady, waiting for one clean signal in the noise.
-> find_signal_puzzle

== hold_hard
set channel_unstable = true
> The channel bucks under Slim's hands. It holds. Barely.
-> find_signal_puzzle

== find_signal_puzzle
puzzle find-signal
    pass -> rustler_expelled
    lockout -> rustler_escaped

== rustler_expelled
# kept: script.rpy:518
rustler: (Sh-clever human sh-this round sh-to you)
show terminal idle right
if channel_unstable
    terminal: Connection stabilized. Barely.
else
    terminal: Connection stable. Channel clear.
-> resolution

== rustler_escaped
> The trace clears half a second too late. Whatever the rustler came for, it's already gone with them.
> The loader itself is sound - coupled, linked, running clean. That much, at least, holds.
-> ending_escaped
